Fix the libcrypto probe against OpenSSL 1.1+/3.x

configure.ac links a trivial program against OpenSSL_add_all_ciphers to
detect libcrypto. OpenSSL 1.1.0 turned that function into a no-op macro
with no exported symbol, so the probe fails to link against any OpenSSL
this new and configure hard-errors:

  checking for OpenSSL_add_all_ciphers in -lcrypto... no
  configure: error: Cannot build without libcrypto (OpenSSL)

xar's own source never calls OpenSSL_add_all_ciphers - the explicit
init it existed for is unnecessary since OpenSSL 1.1 initializes itself -
so the probe only needs a symbol that is still actually exported.
EVP_MD_CTX_new has been present, unchanged, since OpenSSL 1.1.0.

Upstream is inactive (no commits since 2014), so this could not be taken
from a newer release.

diff --git a/xar/configure.ac b/xar/configure.ac
index 812b5ff..954f3e0 100644
--- a/xar/configure.ac
+++ b/xar/configure.ac
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@ dnl Configure libcrypto (part of OpenSSL).
 dnl 
 have_libcrypto="1"
 AC_CHECK_HEADERS([openssl/evp.h], , [have_libcrypto="0"])
-AC_CHECK_LIB([crypto], [OpenSSL_add_all_ciphers], , [have_libcrypto="0"])
+AC_CHECK_LIB([crypto], [EVP_MD_CTX_new], , [have_libcrypto="0"])
 if test "x${have_libcrypto}" = "x0" ; then
   AC_MSG_ERROR([Cannot build without libcrypto (OpenSSL)])
 fi
